# Shell hooks and helper scripts MUST stay LF — a CRLF shebang (#!/bin/sh\r)
# breaks execution under Git Bash ("bad interpreter"). Pin them explicitly so a
# fresh clone / re-checkout on Windows cannot corrupt them.
.claude/githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
.claude/scripts/**/*.py text eol=lf

# BACKLOG generator inputs and outputs MUST stay LF. backlog_gen._write always
# emits newline="\n" while _read round-trips working-tree bytes, and cmd_regen
# decides staleness with a raw `current != text` comparison. Under
# core.autocrlf=true these files are CRLF in the working tree and LF in the
# blob, so on any differently-configured checkout `regen` rewrites whole files
# for line-ending reasons alone and reports them stale with no content change.
# A whole-file diff that is 100% line endings is indistinguishable from one
# that is not, which makes an equivalence gate unclassifiable. The item
# README.md files are pinned for the same reason: they are generator inputs,
# but cmd_status / cmd_register / cmd_renumber also rewrite them through
# _write, so an unpinned README flips to LF the first time its status changes.
Docs/Management/BACKLOG.md text eol=lf
Docs/Management/backlog-archive/*.md text eol=lf
Docs/Management/**/README.md text eol=lf
